<title>ITALY: Shareholder pact broken up at Italy's SAI.</title>
<headline>Shareholder pact broken up at Italy's SAI.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Premafin, a holding company owned by the Ligresti family, said Monday it was pulling out of a shareholders' pact with France's GAN through which the two exercised control over Turin insurer SAI.</p>
<p>Premafin said in a statement the board had agreed at a meeting on Monday to terminate the pact on December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Premafin and Gan had pooled shareholdings in SAI of 42.05 percent and 10 percent respectively in the syndicate. Premafin's total stake in SAI is 43.8 percent, Gan's is 11.21 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
